  "name": "@probitas-test/builder",
  "variant": "project",
  "kind": 1,
  "flags": {},
  "comment": {
    "summary": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Builder module for creating scenario definitions with a fluent, type-safe API.\n\nThis package provides the "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "scenario",
        "target": 24
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " fn function that returns a builder\nfor constructing scenario definitions. The builder uses method chaining to define\nresources, setup functions, and test steps with full TypeScript type inference.\n\n## Links\n\n- [GitHub Repository](https://github.com/probitas-test/probitas)\n- [@probitas-test/probitas](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@probitas-test/probitas) - Main package (recommended for most users)\n\n## Related Packages\n\n| Package | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| [@probitas-test/core](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@probitas-test/core) | Core type definitions used by this builder |\n| [@probitas-test/runner](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@probitas-test/runner) | Executes scenarios built with this package |\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Fluent API**: Chain methods naturally to build complex scenarios\n- **Type-safe context**: Each step receives typed access to previous step results\n- **Resource management**: Register resources with automatic lifecycle handling\n- **Setup/Cleanup**: Define setup functions with automatic cleanup support\n- **Configurable defaults**: Override timeout and retry settings at any level\n\n## Core Exports\n\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "scenario",
        "target": 24
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " - Factory function to create a new scenario builder\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "StepContext"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " - Type representing the context passed to step functions\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "StepFunction"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " - Type signature for step functions\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "SetupFunction"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " - Type signature for setup functions\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "ResourceFunction"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " - Type signature for resource fn functions\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "BuilderScenarioOptions"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " - Partial options for scenario configuration\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "BuilderStepOptions"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " - Partial options for step configuration\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
        "text": "DEFAULT_SCENARIO_OPTIONS"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": " - Default values for scenario options\n- "
      },
      {
        "kind": "inline-tag",
        "tag": "@linkcode",
